! mcp_bootstrap_p209.strap -- MCP printed page 209.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.216, read at 400 dpi, 900 dpi for
! doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
!  CARD ID MA000384  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 209"; the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 222533, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  56 lines, contiguous from 222533.40 to 222602.00.
!   line  22  CNOP printing no location (counter already on a word).
!   line  49  CNUM SYN,12. (prints 000014.00+ +00000000 NULL).
!   line  50  remark continuation card, NAME "-": compiles nothing,
!             not transcribed.
!   line  56  CX (A*)DD(BU,6,6),P* prints a LOCATION and NO binary.
!
! >>> CARD SERIALS. <<<  MA000384 .. MA000431, one per line except
! eight pairs that share a serial: lines 9/10 (392), 11/12 (393),
! 13/14 (394), 24/25 (404), 26/27 (405), 28/29 (406), 45/46 (422),
! 47/48 (423) -- each pair a full/half-word instruction followed by a
! half word, the shape of two statements on one card.  Written here
! one statement per printed line.  Asterisks after the LOCATION on
! lines 5, 8, 23 and 41; recorded, not explained.
!
! >>> "ACP" IS AOP. <<<  LV,14,A?P on lines 9/11/15/24/26/30: the
! middle glyph at 900 dpi is the same squared, upper-right-broken
! round that this page prints as the O of CNOP (line 7) and NOP
! (line 14), not the C of CNOP's first letter.  External; the name
! does not reach the binary.
!
! Octal-field C glyphs (e.g. line 8 "C0C002.CC", line 36 "000C03.10",
! line 49 "+00C00000", "150" printed "15C" on lines 51/52 = 0o226) are
! 0 by the octal rule / the printed count.
!
! >>> HEX BYTES PRINTED WITH AN OPEN ROUND, WRITTEN 0. <<<  Lines 1 and
! 5 print "AC", line 4 "FC", line 27 "C0".  At 900 dpi each is the same
! open round that the same row prints in its OCTAL fields ("224C12.CC",
! "224C20.30 8C", "010000.C6"), where only 0 can stand; and the
! statements cannot make a C: TI/SF carry no second-operand index
! (low nibble 0), B,AXBEE no index (byte 00, as lines 10/25 print it).
!
! >>> $MCP AND $RET WRITTEN AS PRINTED. <<<  Lines 39/43 "B,$MCP" and
! 40/44 ",$RET": MCP pseudo-ops are STRAP system symbols assembled by
! preceding with $ (N28-1081 p.8, in C28-6129 PDF p.66).  Their printed
! binaries 000040.10 00 / 000041.00 80 are exactly what line 47/48's
! B,DMCP / ,DRET print (DMCP 32.0, DRET 33.0 landed).

ALNKMS  SYN, (8)224012.0             ! TI on line 1, BIT-EXACT
CMESS1  SYN, (8)224014.0             ! SF on line 4 (CMESS1+4.24 = 224020.30), BIT-EXACT
AGFM    SYN, (8)222447.40            ! B,AGFM+1. on line 2, half word only
A2FMC   SYN, (8)224005.0             ! LF on line 3, BIT-EXACT
AOP     SYN, (8)224046.0             ! LV on line 9, half word only
ATSWCR  SYN(BU,1), (8)223744.15            ! BB on line 37, BIT-EXACT
ATSWC4  SYN, (8)222472.40            ! BB on line 37, half word only
ATSWC6  SYN, (8)222474.0             ! BB on line 41, half word only
ATARI   SYN(BU,1), (8)223744.13      ! CM1111 on line 38, BIT-EXACT; (BU,1) from its printed 001000.36
ATBRI   SYN(BU,1), (8)223744.12      ! CM1111 on line 42, BIT-EXACT; (BU,1) from its printed 001000.36
CY      SYN, (8)223030.0             ! CW on line 52, BIT-EXACT
DMCP    SYN, 32.0                    ! landed
DRET    SYN, 33.0                    ! landed

        SLC, (8)222533.40
        TI,2,ALNKMS,CMESS1                                   ! line  1
        B,AGFM+1.                                            ! line  2
AERRUN  LF(BU,8),A2FMC                                       ! line  3
        SF(BU,8),CMESS1+4.24                                 ! line  4
        TI,2,ALNKMS,CMESS1                                   ! line  5
        B,AGFM+1.                                            ! line  6
        CNOP,                                                ! line  7
AXITA   DRZ(N),2                                             ! line  8
        LV,14,AOP                                            ! line  9
        B,AXAUK                                              ! line 10
        LV,14,AOP                                            ! line 11
        B,AXAEE                                              ! line 12
        B,RATPCS                                             ! line 13
        NOP,                                                 ! line 14
        LV,14,AOP                                            ! line 15
        TI,2,AXITA,0($14)                                    ! line 16
        B,5.($14)                                            ! line 17
AXAUK   TI,2,AXITA,0($14)                                    ! line 18
        B,2.($14)                                            ! line 19
AXAEE   TI,2,AXITA,($14)                                     ! line 20
        B,3.($14)                                            ! line 21
        CNOP,                                                ! line 22
AXITB   DRZ(N),2                                             ! line 23
        LV,14,AOP                                            ! line 24
        B,AXBUK                                              ! line 25
        LV,14,AOP                                            ! line 26
        B,AXBEE                                              ! line 27
        B,ATPBCS                                             ! line 28
        NOP,                                                 ! line 29
        LV,14,AOP                                            ! line 30
        TI,2,AXITB,0($14)                                    ! line 31
        B,5.($14)                                            ! line 32
AXBUK   TI,2,AXITB,0($14)                                    ! line 33
        B,2.($14)                                            ! line 34
AXBEE   TI,2,AXITB,0($14)                                    ! line 35
        B,3.($14)                                            ! line 36
ATPACS  BB,ATSWCR,ATSWC4                                     ! line 37
        CM1111,ATARI                                         ! line 38
        B,$MCP                                               ! line 39
        ,$RET                                                ! line 40
ATPBCS  BB,ATSWCR,ATSWC6                                     ! line 41
        CM1111,ATBRI                                         ! line 42
        B,$MCP                                               ! line 43
        ,$RET                                                ! line 44
RATPCS  LVI,14,ATPACS                                        ! line 45
        SVA,14,AXITA+4.0                                     ! line 46
        B,DMCP                                               ! line 47
        ,DRET                                                ! line 48
CNUM    SYN,12.                                              ! line 49  -THIS PARAMETER CAN BE VARIED
CWX     CW(CR),CX,150,CWX                                    ! line 51  -CWS FOR BUFFERS X AND Y
CWY     CW(CR),CY,150,CWY                                    ! line 52  -CF=X+1.
CWA     XW,CX+.6,CNUM,CWW                                    ! line 53  -TRANSMISSION INDEX
CWT     XW,CX+.6,CNUM,CWW                                    ! line 54  -BUFFER X
CWW     XW,CY+.6,CNUM,CWT                                    ! line 55  -BUFFER Y
CX      (A*)DD(BU,6,6),P*                                    ! line 56  -BUFFER X AND Y RESERVATION

!SYM AERRUN 222535.00
!SYM AXITA  222541.00
!SYM AXAUK  222550.00
!SYM AXAEE  222551.40
!SYM AXITB  222553.00
